{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540103-are-vows-bad","id":1540103,"title":"Are vows bad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-09T15:00:16-07:00","id":1540103,"title":"Are vows bad?","content":"Aside from narrative flavour, what you get for maintaining a vow seems to be one mana per week and the ability to break it for a free +2 Yantra. I wish you'd get a free reach on a thematic practice for maintaining it or something. Ideas on improving it? Maybe you get more effects the longer you maintain it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T15:56:35-07:00","id":1540106,"title":"","content":"Maybe have them apply dice modifiers. An example is a Guardian who killed twice recently, and while they believe taking on that burden is part of their role, they feel they didn't do all they could. So they take a vow of Pacifism, forcing them to think of alternatives. Suddenly they get a positive modifier in social interactions with the Vidantus, Plain or other pacifists.<br /> <br /> A Silver Ladder mentor wants their pupil to elevate their capability for reflection and communication to the next level, so they take a vow of Silence. Now the silence in their words and stillness in their thoughts echo Stygia's own, so having them in a summoning area for beings of that Realm provides a bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T18:26:18-07:00","id":1540114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hydrophiliak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540103-are-vows-bad#post1540103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from narrative flavour, what you get for maintaining a vow seems to be one mana per week and the ability to break it for a free +2 Yantra. I wish you'd get a free reach on a thematic practice for maintaining it or something. Ideas on improving it? Maybe you get more effects the longer you maintain it?</div> </div> </div> </div>On top of giving you a Beat as the resolution of a Condition, you get Willpower when you break a vow nonmagically and breaking it with a spell is a Yantra that doesn't count against your Gnosis-based limit and lets you roll your casting pool twice and take the better result. You get Mana from vows without needing to go to a Hallow, belong to a Legacy, resolve an Obsession, or take it from somewhere else, and vows can be relatively simple to keep despite their impact on the character's life.<br /> <br /> Simply making the decision to go without worldly luxuries or compulsively gamble or assume a new identity only has the described mechanical effects, but it's very easy to hook that vow into one's Shadow Name or Obsessions or even a Legacy. If you want a character to get more out of vows alone, setting up a cheap Merit that enhances the benefits of upholding a particular type of vow (in exchange for worse consequences from breaking it) is one of the most straightforward ways to build on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T16:13:54-07:00","id":1540152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540103-are-vows-bad?p=1540106#post1540106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe have them apply dice modifiers. An example is a Guardian who killed twice recently, and while they believe taking on that burden is part of their role, they feel they didn't do all they could. So they take a vow of Pacifism, forcing them to think of alternatives. Suddenly they get a positive modifier in social interactions with the Vidantus, Plain or other pacifists.<br /> <br /> A Silver Ladder mentor wants their pupil to elevate their capability for reflection and communication to the next level, so they take a vow of Silence. Now the silence in their words and stillness in their thoughts echo Stygia's own, so having them in a summoning area for beings of that Realm provides a bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of keeping the benefits really niche and themed, I didn't even think of non-magic benefits. It's a pretty cool way of narratively getting a dot in something by taking a vow and then using experience to buy it so it permanently becomes part of your character even after you break it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T11:44:03-07:00","id":1540213,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think a vow that does more has to have a deeper buy in, because otherwise it seems a lot like a game of tailoring a vow that doesn't really give up anything a player would care to keep anyway in exchange for some all around bonus, at which point it becomes an optimisation mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T13:08:26-07:00","id":1540219,"title":"","content":"I don't see vows as bad, but not to be taken lightly as you can get blowback if you don't uphold it at all. But to be fair I'm approaching this from the angle of Changeling The Lost 1st Edition as the Wyrd can be very demanding if you take up pledges and oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:50:17-07:00","id":1540232,"title":"","content":"I think changeling makes them more interesting, to be honest.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of taking a vow as a part of casting a spell to get extra duration for as long as you hold the vow.<br /> Like, I have shifted the leylines in this area for as long as I don't use my eyes or somesuch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T17:33:27-07:00","id":1540245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hydrophiliak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540103-are-vows-bad?p=1540232#post1540232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of taking a vow as a part of casting a spell to get extra duration for as long as you hold the vow.<br /> Like, I have shifted the leylines in this area for as long as I don't use my eyes or somesuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem it that that's just Conditional Duration, which has its own mechanics that can be used for more than just self-imposed restrictions on one's own way of living.<br /> <br /> I'm getting vibes of the old &quot;Sanctum is underwhelming&quot; discussion, which runs into the same problem where Merits exist in the context of a game where you can get a very flexible and very potentially powerful expansion of your kit for as much Experience as a four-dot Merit and that seemingly throws off expectations for what a Merit is balanced to do.<br /> <br /> Granted, that same discussion came down on the end of &quot;since it's basically impossible to make Merits mechanically superior to Arcanum dots without breaking the intended balance over your knee, appealing Mage Merits are ones that add interesting new features,&quot; but given that vows are a free template feature that have already been expanded in scope from their 1e mechanics in Tome of the Watchtowers of simply giving you a point of Mana for every week you remained dedicated, I don't know that there's much to reasonably apply intrinsically to the mechanic that doesn't mess with 2e's heightened Mana scarcity or step on the toes of existing Merits, spells, and other systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T04:09:46-07:00","id":1540267,"title":"","content":"I'd maybe up the mana output to 1 per day? That's potentially quite a lot, but the example oaths are all asking quite a lot of the individual so I think we can balance it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T14:53:58-07:00","id":1540300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540103-are-vows-bad?p=1540267#post1540267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd maybe up the mana output to 1 per day? That's potentially quite a lot, but the example oaths are all asking quite a lot of the individual so I think we can balance it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a mana each time the vow seriously inconveniences you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T15:15:15-07:00","id":1540304,"title":"","content":"In the case of a vote of pacifism, for example, I don't think it would maintain the theme if you incentivize the character under oath to provoke others and sow chaos. I think a point of mana per day might work, it might not be so bad in cases where the cabal is active for multiple days in a row.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T11:37:15-07:00","id":1540374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540103-are-vows-bad?p=1540304#post1540304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of a vote of pacifism, for example, I don't think it would maintain the theme if you incentivize the character under oath to provoke others and sow chaos. I think a point of mana per day might work, it might not be so bad in cases where the cabal is active for multiple days in a row.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more like when a situation would easily call for violence and you uphold your oath, you'd gain a mana. The storyteller would be the one provoking you rather than the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}